RISC-V: an unrolled copy from a field of a local at an unaligned offset is copied byte-wise.

Without unaligned access (JitNoUnalignedAccess) an unrolled block copy is marked unaligned when one
of its addresses is not known to be aligned for the pieces of the copy, and is then copied byte by
byte. A source that is a local was taken as aligned: a frame slot is. A field of the local is at any
offset that its own alignment allows - a struct of bytes inside a packed struct, the value of a
Nullable<T> of one - and the copy read it in pieces of up to a register. The offset of the source
within the local is now compared with the piece size, as the offset of an address is.

Regression test: bflat-ts:memory/inline_object_alloc

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
@@ -10826,6 +10826,19 @@ void Lowering::LowerCopyBlockStore(GenTreeBlk* blkNode)
         {
             ContainBlockStoreAddress(blkNode, size, src->AsIndir()->Addr(), src->AsIndir());
         }
+#ifdef TARGET_RISCV64
+        else if ((JitConfig.JitNoUnalignedAccess() != 0) && src->OperIsLocalRead())
+        {
+            // A local is at an aligned frame slot, but a field of it is at any offset that its own
+            // alignment allows (a struct of bytes in a packed struct, the value of a Nullable<T> of
+            // one), and the unrolled copy reads it in pieces of up to a register.
+            const unsigned pieceSize = (size >= REGSIZE_BYTES) ? REGSIZE_BYTES : (size >= 4) ? 4 : (size >= 2) ? 2 : 1;
+            if ((src->AsLclVarCommon()->GetLclOffs() % pieceSize) != 0)
+            {
+                blkNode->gtFlags |= GTF_IND_UNALIGNED;
+            }
+        }
+#endif // TARGET_RISCV64
         ContainBlockStoreAddress(blkNode, size, dstAddr, nullptr);
         return;
     }
